const COMMIT_MSG = `fix(hono): unify worker/jobs routes to the durable-queue storage

The /api/ivx/senior-developer/worker/jobs POST and GET /:taskId routes at
line 3116-3117 used handleSeniorDevWorkerSubmit/Status from
ivx-senior-dev-worker.ts, which read from the ivx_owner_ai_tasks Supabase
table. But the IVX IA Chat path (ivx-owner-ai.ts self_developer branch)
enqueues via enqueueOrAttachSeniorDeveloperJob from
ivx-senior-developer-worker.ts, which uses a DIFFERENT storage (in-memory +
GitHub side-branch durable queue + Supabase durable store).

Result: a job created from chat appeared in the dashboard list (which reads
the durable queue) but GET /jobs/:taskId returned 404 (because the status
handler read from the wrong table). The chat E2E test confirmed: taskId
extracted, task in dashboard list, but GET 404.

Fix: point both routes at the unified handlers
(handleSeniorDeveloperWorkerEnqueueRequest / handleSeniorDeveloperWorkerJobRequest)
imported at line 791, which read from the same durable queue the chat path
writes to. The approve route stays as handleSeniorDevWorkerApprove (separate
concern, reads from ivx_owner_ai_tasks which is where approvals are recorded).`;

console.log("\n=== COMMIT: hono.ts (gzip-base64) ===");
